gal help it  takes coordinating with the office of  public affairs and communications as  well as aya to get the messaging out  there so it really is a team of people  needed to mount one of these courses and  it's a lot of work especially the first  time around so what we're hoping is that  if any of the faculty members are  willing to offer the course a second or  third time that we will see a little  it'll s work the second or third time  because we'll have videos created will  have the core structures in place but  the first time we have to be clear it is  a lot of work for everyone involved  secondly this is what we're talking  about with teaching assistants I didn't  use the term just because we're not  exactly sure about title so we'll just  focus on what it is the graduate  students who are helping us in these  courses the lead faculty member needs  very strong teaching and academic  support on the other ends things like  technical or administration we are  helping the faculty member from that  respect but each faculty member has a  teaching fellow to help them think about  core structure to help them manage the  message boards and help them engage in  the course I think what's interesting  about this is as Sarah said you know the  best way to give experiences to or to  gain experience is to give experience  and perhaps these MOOCs offer us new  ways to provide graduate students just  small slivers of experience in online  teaching now one of our faculty members  made a great point last week when we  were talking about this idea of teaching  support he said what I find is someone  who would make a great teaching  assistant in the classroom is likely to  make a great teaching assistant online  but if you think about that a little bit  more I think there's one other aspect to  this and that there are other  opportunities for that teaching  assistant to think about technology so  how do you really manage a discussion  forum how do you pose a question to get  a 